## Why This Is Asked

This question tests your understanding of counting DP, covering both memoization (top-down) and tabulation (bottom-up) approaches, along with space optimization and edge-case handling.

## Key Concepts

- Subset sum counting with each element used at most once
- Memoization (top-down) with recursive DFS and memo table
- Tabulation (bottom-up) with 1D space optimization to O(S)
- Modulo arithmetic to prevent integer overflow

## Edge Cases

- **Empty subset (N=0)**: If N=0 and S=0, return 1 (one valid subset - empty set). If S>0, return 0.
- **Target S=0**: Always return 1 (the empty subset counts as one valid subset).
- **All elements greater than S**: No valid subsets exist, return 0.

## Code Example

```javascript
function countSubsets(nums, target) {
  const mod = 1_000_000_007;
  const n = nums.length;

  // Top-down with memoization
  const memo = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(target + 1).fill(-1));
  function dfs(i, s) {
    if (s === 0) return 1;
    if (i === 0) return 0;
    if (memo[i][s] !== -1) return memo[i][s];
    memo[i][s] = dfs(i - 1, s) % mod;
    if (s >= nums[i - 1]) {
      memo[i][s] = (memo[i][s] + dfs(i - 1, s - nums[i - 1])) % mod;
    }
    return memo[i][s];
  }
  return dfs(n, target);
}

// Bottom-up with space optimization
function countSubsetsBU(nums, target) {
  const mod = 1_000_000_007;
  const dp = Array(target + 1).fill(0);
  dp[0] = 1;

  for (const num of nums) {
    for (let s = target; s >= num; s--) {
      dp[s] = (dp[s] + dp[s - num]) % mod;
    }
  }
  return dp[target];
}
```

Both solutions run in O(N×S) time with the bottom-up approach using O(S) space.

## Why This Is Asked

Models real build/dependency graphs where costs accumulate; asks for both memoized and tabular DP to compare patterns and understand trade-offs. Emphasizes modulo arithmetic and edge-case handling for unreachable sinks and tight budgets.

## Key Concepts

- DP on DAG with an extra weight dimension
- Top-down memoization with (node, remainingBudget)
- Bottom-up DP in topological order with weight axis
- Modulo arithmetic and edge-case handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Top-down memoized DFS
function countPaths(n, edges, W) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) adj[u].push([v, w]);
  const memo = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(W + 1).fill(-1));
  const dfs = (u, rem) => {
    if (u === n - 1) return 1;
    if (memo[u][rem] !== -1) return memo[u][rem];
    let res = 0;
    for (const [v, w] of adj[u]) if (w <= rem) res = (res + dfs(v, rem - w)) % 1_000_000_007;
    return memo[u][rem] = res;
  };
  return dfs(0, W);
}
```

```javascript
// Bottom-up DP in topological order
function countPathsBottomUp(n, edges, W) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) {
    adj[u].push([v, w]);
    indeg[v]++;
  }
  // Kahn's algorithm for topo order
  const q = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  const topo = [];
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift(); topo.push(u);
    for (const [v] of adj[u]) if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(W + 1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 1;
  for (const u of topo) {
    for (const [v, w] of adj[u]) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= W - w; t++) {
        if (dp[u][t] !== 0) dp[v][t + w] = (dp[v][t + w] + dp[u][t]) % 1_000_000_007;
      }
    }
  }
  let ans = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= W; t++) ans = (ans + dp[n - 1][t]) % 1_000_000_007;
  return ans;
}
```

